---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms &amp; Conditions | Harrow &amp; Thread"
  description="Terms and conditions for bespoke hand-woven rug, wall hanging and wall-to-wall carpet commissions."
>
  <section class="section-pad">
    <div class="shell max-w-narrow">
      <h1 class="display text-3xl xs:text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl text-ink mb-5 reveal">
        Terms &amp; Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-graphite mb-12">Last updated: 14 September 2026</p>

      <!-- Consumer (B2C) -->
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink mb-6">Consumer (B2C)</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">The Harrow &amp; Thread Exclusivity Guarantee</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-4">
        <strong>One-of-One Policy:</strong> Every custom design created for a client is exclusive. We will never recreate your specific design for another customer.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        <strong>Design Privacy:</strong> Your custom design will not be sold, licensed, or repurposed for any other Harrow &amp; Thread projects.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Intellectual Property</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        The design is yours. On final payment we assign to you, in writing, the copyright and design rights in the design created for your commission. We keep no right to reuse, license or sell it. If you would like it entered on the UK register of designs, we will file the application for you and the registration fee is included: registration lasts five years, and is yours to renew in five-year steps to twenty-five. Copyright itself arises automatically on creation and needs no registration. The client retains ownership of any original artwork, sketches or reference images they provide.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Deposit and Payment Terms</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-2">
        <strong>Deposit:</strong> Once you have approved the design, a 50% deposit is required to confirm your order. Production usually begins within 12 to 24 hours of receiving the deposit. The deposit is refundable in full until production begins, and non-refundable from the point production begins.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        <strong>Final Balance:</strong> The remaining 50% balance must be paid in full prior to shipping.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Bespoke Goods and Cancellation Rights</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        Your order is for bespoke goods made to your personal specification. Under the Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013, you do not have the right to cancel this order once production has commenced. Your statutory rights under the Consumer Rights Act 2015, including the short-term right to reject and the six-month period for latent faults, are unaffected.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Production and Specifications</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-4">
        As each piece is handmade, slight variations in colour and texture are a natural characteristic. Colour is matched to the ARS 1,400 colour system reference you select. Physical dyed wool may vary slightly from a screen render.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        Standard production and delivery timeframe is approximately six to seven (6-7) weeks from Order Sign-Off. Complex designs, larger sizes or specific material requirements may extend the timeline.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Wall-to-Wall Carpets: Measurement and Trimming</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-2">
        <strong>Measurement Responsibility:</strong> You supply the two longest measurements of the room. You are responsible for the accuracy of their measurements. A professional measure is recommended.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-2">
        <strong>Charged Area:</strong> You are charged for the full rectangle, including trimming waste. The charged area is disclosed in the proposal before the deposit is taken.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-2">
        <strong>Fitting:</strong> Carpets are supplied only. The carpet arrives oversized and requires a fitter to trim and fit to the room. UK fitting can be arranged on request.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        <strong>Pattern Trimming:</strong> The design is centred to the ordered rectangle. Trimming at a bay or chimney breast will cut into the pattern.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Wall Hangings: Hanging and Fixings</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-2">
        No pole, rail, fixings or hardware are supplied. You are responsible for hanging the piece and for the suitability of their fixings and wall.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        Weight per square metre at each pile height is stated in your proposal. You are responsible for ensuring their wall and fixings can support the weight of the piece.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Shipping and Transit Protection</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-4">
        We provide full-value transit insurance on every shipment at our own expense. If your piece is lost or damaged in transit, we will manage the insurance claim and prioritise a replacement.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-4">
        Shipping is included in your price for most commissions. Exceptionally large or heavy pieces may carry an additional freight charge, passed on at cost and stated in your proposal, before you commit to the deposit.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        Following the UK-India trade deal that took effect in July 2026, UK deliveries no
        longer carry import duty. For deliveries outside the UK, import duty and local
        VAT remain the client's responsibility.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Product Care and Liability</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        A care guide specific to your chosen fibres will be provided. Harrow &amp; Thread is not responsible for damage caused by improper cleaning, failure to follow care instructions, or use of the piece in unsuitable environments.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Colour Variance Acknowledgement</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-12">
        At sign-off, the client must actively acknowledge that physical dyed wool may vary slightly from a screen render, and that the ARS colour reference is authoritative.
      </p>

      <!-- Business (B2B) -->
      <h2 class="display text-2xl text-ink mb-6">Business (B2B)</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Applicability</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        These Terms apply to all orders placed by business clients, trade clients, interior designers, and commercial entities.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">The Harrow &amp; Thread Exclusivity Guarantee</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        Every custom design created for a client is exclusive. We will not recreate your specific design for any other customer without your prior written consent.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Intellectual Property</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite mb-8">
        The design is yours. On final payment we assign to you, in writing, the copyright and design rights in the design created for your commission. We keep no right to reuse, license or sell it. If you would like it entered on the UK register of designs, we will file the application for you and the registration fee is included: registration lasts five years, and is yours to renew in five-year steps to twenty-five. Copyright itself arises automatically on creation and needs no registration.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg text-ink font-medium mb-2">Limitation of Liability</h3>
      <p class="text-base text-graphite">
        Harrow &amp; Thread's total liability shall not exceed the total price paid for that order. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>